      "note": "BATTLE OF TEN KINGS (दशराज युद्ध) ⭐\n│\n├── 📌 Time\n│   └── Around 1500 BCE (Rigvedic Period)\n│\n├── 📖 Source\n│   └── Rigveda (7th Mandala) ⭐\n│       └── Associated with → Rishi Vashistha ⭐\n│\n├── ⚔️ Participants\n│   │\n│   ├── 🟢 Bharata Tribe (Winner) ⭐\n│   │   └── King → Sudas ⭐\n│   │\n│   └── 🔴 Confederacy of Tribes\n│       ├── Puru\n│       ├── Yadu\n│       ├── Turvasha\n│       ├── Anu\n│       ├── Druhyu\n│       └── + other tribes\n│\n├── 📍 Location\n│   └── River Parushni ⭐\n│       └── Present → Ravi River\n│\n├── ⚔️ Cause\n│   ├── Inter-tribal rivalry\n│   ├── Struggle for power & territory\n│   └── Conflict among Aryan tribes\n│\n├── 🏆 Result\n│   ├── Sudas defeated the confederacy ⭐\n│   └── Rise of Bharata dominance\n│\n├── 🧠 Importance ⭐\n│   ├── Early example of tribal warfare\n│   ├── Shows political structure of Rigvedic age\n│   └── Strengthened Bharata tribe\n│\n├── 📖 NCERT Story ⭐\n│   ├── Many tribes lived in north-west India during Vedic period\n│   ├── Sudas, king of Bharata tribe, was guided by priest Vashistha\n│   ├── Earlier, Vishvamitra was associated with Sudas\n│   ├── Later conflict arose between Vishvamitra and Sudas\n│   ├── Vishvamitra supported rival tribes against Sudas\n│   ├── Several tribes formed a confederacy (दशराज)\n│   ├── Battle took place on River Parushni\n│   ├── Sudas defeated the combined forces\n│   └── Bharatas emerged as the dominant tribe"
    },
